<!--
FastDDS without the shared-memory transport.

WHY THIS EXISTS
Fast DDS defaults to shared memory between processes on one host, and on this
stack that transport stops accepting new participants once the sim has been up
for a while. The symptom is specific and it wasted a lot of time: the nodes
that were launched together keep talking to each other perfectly — the drone
flies, MAVROS gets its pose — while ANY process that joins later receives
nothing at all. `ros2 topic list` still shows all 176 topics, because discovery
works; only the data never arrives.

rviz2 is exactly such a late joiner. That is why its displays go red and empty,
why the octomap "flickers", and why topics appear to vanish.

MEASURED 2026-08-26, a fresh subscriber inside the running container, 20 s:

                                  with SHM     UDP only
    /tf                                  0            1
    /octomap_binary                      0           33
    /hydrone/map/cloud_filtered          0           32
    cloud_registered (the source)        0           36

Clearing the 386 orphaned /dev/shm/fastrtps_* segments left over from previous
runs (97 MB, none in use) did NOT help, so it is not simply stale files.

THE COST
UDP loopback copies where shared memory would not, so large messages pay for
it. The biggest thing on this bus is the ZED cloud at ~230 KB per frame, 10 Hz
-> ~2.3 MB/s over lo. That is nothing for loopback, and it is worth paying to
have a bus that works.

ON THE HOST
rviz2 and any `ros2` command outside the container need this too:
    export FASTRTPS_DEFAULT_PROFILES_FILE=<repo>/docker/fastdds_udp_only.xml
scripts/env.sh does it for you.
-->
<dds xmlns="http://www.eprosima.com">
  <profiles>
    <transport_descriptors>
      <transport_descriptor>
        <transport_id>udp_transport</transport_id>
        <type>UDPv4</type>
      </transport_descriptor>
    </transport_descriptors>

    <participant profile_name="udp_only" is_default_profile="true">
      <rtps>
        <userTransports>
          <transport_id>udp_transport</transport_id>
        </userTransports>
        <!-- false, or Fast DDS adds the shared-memory transport back -->
        <useBuiltinTransports>false</useBuiltinTransports>
      </rtps>
    </participant>
  </profiles>
</dds>
